# Brandon Deurbrouck — Photography

## Adding your photos

Drop images into the `images/` folder with these exact filenames:

| File | Where it appears |
|------|-----------------|
| `hero.jpg` | Hero section (full height, right side) |
| `photo-1.jpg` | Gallery — large left tile |
| `photo-2.jpg` | Gallery — top right |
| `photo-3.jpg` | Gallery — top far right |
| `photo-4.jpg` | Gallery — bottom right |
| `photo-5.jpg` | Gallery — bottom far right |
| `photo-6.jpg` | Gallery row |
| `photo-7.jpg` | Gallery row |
| `photo-8.jpg` | Gallery row |
| `photo-9.jpg` | Gallery row |
| `print-1.jpg` | Prints shop — card 1 |
| `print-2.jpg` | Prints shop — card 2 |
| `print-3.jpg` | Prints shop — card 3 |
| `about.jpg` | About section portrait |

**Tips:**
- `hero.jpg` — portrait or landscape, at least 1400px tall
- Gallery featured tiles — any orientation works, at least 1200px wide
- Gallery row — portrait (3:4) looks best
- Print cards — portrait (4:5) ratio

## Connecting Shopify

In `index.html`, find the three `YOUR-SHOPIFY-STORE` placeholders and replace with your actual Shopify store URL and product slugs.

## Deploy

```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/brandon-deurbrouck.git
git push -u origin main
```

Then in Vercel: import the repo, framework = Other, deploy. Since your domain is registered with Vercel, add `www.brandondeurbrouck.com` under Settings → Domains and it auto-configures.

## File structure
```
bd-final/
├── index.html
├── vercel.json
├── .gitignore
└── images/
    ├── hero.jpg
    ├── photo-1.jpg ... photo-9.jpg
    ├── print-1.jpg ... print-3.jpg
    └── about.jpg
```
